# {{.Name}}

Run `graft dev`, then open http://localhost:8080 and http://localhost:8080/swagger.
Use `graft build` for a local binary or `graft publish --target linux-x64` to deploy.

Configuration uses environment variables directly. `.env.example` is a reference;
Graft does not load it automatically. Set `APP_PORT` and, for migrations,
`DATABASE_URL` in your shell or service configuration.

Create SQL with `graft make:migration create_machines_table`, edit the Up/Down
sections, then run `graft migrate`. Inspect `graft migrate:status`; undo the most
recent batch with `graft migrate:rollback`, or individual migrations with `--step N`.
Applied migrations must not be edited or removed.

Development-generated projects may have a local `replace` in go.mod. Before
sharing, replace it with your published Graft module/version and run `go mod tidy`.
